      "content": "1. Anonymity (POL-ANO): Verify explicit double-blind markers (e.g., 'Anonymous authors', 'Paper under double-blind review') and scan for self-identifying text, acknowledgments, or URLs. 2. Data Privacy (POL-DAT): Assess datasets for PII; standard public benchmarks (e.g., MNIST) are generally compliant, but sensitive data requires explicit consent and anonymization checks. 3. Broader Impact (POL-IMP): Check for dedicated sections on societal impact, especially for security-related topics like adversarial robustness; flag missing or boilerplate statements as weaknesses. 4. Ethics (POL-ETH): Identify dual-use potential (e.g., attack/defense trade-offs) and ensure authors discuss potential harms or responsible deployment, even for benign tasks. 5. Plagiarism (POL-PLG): Verify proper citation of prior work and originality of empirical findings; look for evidence of dual submission or uncredited reuse.",
